<h3 data-start=3D"64" data-end=3D"127">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F <strong data-star=
t=3D"71" data-end=3D"127">The imported value is NOT USED anywhere in the fi=
le.</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"129" data-end=3D"170">This is normal in one specific situa=
tion:</p>
<p data-start=3D"172" data-end=3D"245">=F0=9F=91=89 <strong data-start=3D"1=
75" data-end=3D"245">If your component file does NOT actually use the <code=
 data-start=3D"226" data-end=3D"233">React</code> variable.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"247" data-end=3D"401">Since React 17+, importing React is =
<strong data-start=3D"283" data-end=3D"305">no longer required</strong> for=
 JSX.<br data-start=3D"314" data-end=3D"317">
So VS Code shows it faded because the import is <strong data-start=3D"365" =
data-end=3D"375">unused</strong>, not because it is wrong.</p>
<p data-start=3D"403" data-end=3D"424">This is NOT an error.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"426" data-end=3D"429">
<h1 data-start=3D"431" data-end=3D"475">=E2=9C=85 But we must confirm somet=
hing important:</h1>
<p data-start=3D"477" data-end=3D"525">If <code data-start=3D"480" data-end=
=3D"508">import React from "react";</code> is faded inside:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"543">=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"533=
" data-end=3D"543">App.js</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"544" data-end=3D"627">=E2=86=92 That is perfectly normal, =
because App.js uses only <code data-start=3D"597" data-end=3D"615">&lt;Reac=
t.Fragment&gt;</code> implicitly.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"629" data-end=3D"661">=E2=9D=97 <strong data-start=3D"635=
" data-end=3D"661">ServiceTypeAnalysis.js</strong></h3>
