<p data-start=3D"351" data-end=3D"395">does <strong data-start=3D"356" data=
-end=3D"363">NOT</strong> do =E2=80=9Cnot cancelled=E2=80=9D.<br data-start=
=3D"383" data-end=3D"386">
It means:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"397" data-end=3D"524">
<p data-start=3D"399" data-end=3D"524"><em data-start=3D"399" data-end=3D"5=
24">status field exists AND its value does not match the regex =E2=80=94 bu=
t only if the field is a string and certain operators apply.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"526" data-end=3D"597">MongoDB does <strong data-start=3D"5=
39" data-end=3D"546">not</strong> support <code data-start=3D"555" data-end=
=3D"561">$not</code> inside <code data-start=3D"569" data-end=3D"577">$matc=
h</code> this way for regex.</p>
<p data-start=3D"599" data-end=3D"722">So entries with <code data-start=3D"=
615" data-end=3D"628">"Cancelled"</code> or <code data-start=3D"632" data-e=
nd=3D"645">"cancelled"</code> are <strong data-start=3D"650" data-end=3D"68=
0">not filtered out correctly</strong>, and some valid rows are removed ins=
tead.</p>
